Replaced the 65536-entry pointer table with a 65536-entry `FIT_UINT16` index table (0 = invalid), shrinking the lookup table from 512 KB to 128 KB so the full-domain sweep stays in L2 cache. The hot path is now a single 16-bit load plus a predictable null check.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static FIT_UINT16 lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (__builtin_expect(!initialized, 0))
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(i + 1);
        initialized = true;
    }

    const FIT_UINT16 idx = lookup[num];
    return idx ? &mesgs[idx - 1] : nullptr;
}
```